            "html": "Create a story, preview it, and save it as a draft or publish it. The dashboard shows recent stories and publication counts. Titles, short stories, and full stories can be edited later."
          },
          {
            "html": "The page also works as an include, so you can show published stories elsewhere on your site:"
          },
          {
            "label": "Include a news feed",
            "code": "<?js await include('./news.cow', {\n  mode: 'feed',\n  url: '/news',\n  limit: 5\n}) ?>"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "source",
        "title": "Read the source",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "html": "Open your copied <code>site/news.cow</code>. It contains the routes, database queries, forms, and markup. The README in <code>node_modules/@cowlang/cow/examples/mininews/</code> covers setup, backups, and embedding."
          },
          {
            "html": "MiniNews stores its database beside the page, under a private underscore-prefixed name. Keep that database when updating the page. Use HTTPS before accepting real logins."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "related": [
      "forms",
      "sessions",
      "sqlite",
      "modules"
    ]
  },
  {
    "slug": "forum",
    "title": "Cow Commons",
    "description": "A forum with accounts, discussions, replies, and moderation.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "id": "run",
        "title": "Run it locally",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "html": "<a href=\"/docs/get-started\">Install Cow locally</a> in a project with an empty <code>site/</code> directory. Copy the contents of <code>node_modules/@cowlang/cow/examples/forum/site/</code> into it, and copy <code>node_modules/@cowlang/cow/examples/forum/setup.mjs</code> into the project root."
          },
          {
            "label": "Terminal — project root",
            "code": "node setup.mjs\nnpm exec --offline -- cow site --port 8002 --workers 2"
          },
          {
            "html": "Visit <code>http://127.0.0.1:8002/install</code>. Use the private key printed by setup to create an administrator. There are no default credentials. Setup creates <code>data/</code> beside <code>site/</code>. Keep it outside the served directory."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "use",
        "title": "Start a discussion",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "html": "Members can register, start topics, reply, and edit their own posts. Administrators can lock topics and remove posts. Readers can browse without an account."
          },
          {
            "html": "Forms work without client-side JavaScript. Sessions and forum data are stored in SQLite, outside the served directory."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "source",
        "title": "Read the source",
        "blocks": [
          {
